meta {
  name: Delete Connection (Undeclared)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/connections/REPLACE_WITH_CONNECTION_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against the connection created in "Create
  Connection.bru" (id `6a9f1cc92b6fd055ffb7c7fe`, since deleted). This was
  the **first** resource where the undeclared-DELETE pattern was
  discovered this session -- `204`, then `404` on a follow-up `GET`
  (`{"errors":[{"name":"NotFoundError","description":"Document with id
  ... not found"}]}`) and a follow-up subpath `GET` (`404
  {"errors":[{"name":"NotFoundError","description":"Resource not
  found"}]}`). `openapi_pimv3.json` declares no `DELETE` for this resource
  at all. Confirmed generalizing to every other Phase 1 resource -- see
  each folder's own "Delete ... (Undeclared)" file.
}
